# Upwork / proposal writing style

When drafting Upwork proposals, cover letters, or client-facing copy for Atharva:

- Never use em dashes (—). Use hyphen `-` or arrow `->` instead.
- Prefer `->` for sequences and cause-effect (e.g. `read guide -> provision infra -> wire env vars`).
- Keep tone direct and human. Avoid polished "AI brochure" phrasing.
- No portfolio links in proposals unless asked; offer samples after NDA via Upwork messages.
- No contact details (email, phone, external links) before contract per Upwork policy.
